{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiWdtobiCUhhCbykUzap","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Taa2u832tLH8uqXJdxTrkW","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"~/.claude/projects/-private-tmp-claude-502-<proj>/memory/laya-step2-lessons.md","content":"---\nname: laya-step2-lessons\ndescription: Laya weight-edit lab step 2 (card PIN -> cards): working recipe, scripts, and the mistakes that cost time\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nStep 2 done 2026-11-04. Final: K=512 whitened PCA, theta 0, cap +8, 5 AND-ed checks (rspbq) on the cards option. Held-out 53/58 PIN, 0/714 false route changes, non-cards logits move exactly 0. Scripts: step-2 session scratchpad `w/` (build.py with generic min_tree, evalc.py summary line, sweep.py, leakcheck.py with keep() filter). Builds on [[laya-marker-vector-geometry]].\n\nLessons:\n- A narrow negative set hides false alarms. Train against a broad set covering ~75 banking request types (broad_msgs.py, even half train, odd half held out). Banking77 test = 3,080 = the hidden set size.\n- Always add a check \"target option vs other options, ALL messages\". Without it the module fired on the fees_fx option (+2.2) of an unrelated message.\n- Track \"max non-cards logit move\" in the eval summary; route-only counts missed that leak.\n- Random template generators: assert the target count fits the unique frames, or the loop hangs.\n- Do not name scripts after stdlib modules (inspect.py broke numpy import). evidence.csv is tab-separated.\n- Shell: `for` loops and `VAR=...; $VAR` need approval here; use a Python driver (sweep.py) instead.\n\n**Why:** step 3 adds one more correction on top; it must keep steps 1 and 2 true.\n**How to apply:** start from step-2 scorer_out.npz; build.py pads old modules with identity layers and stacks the new one block-diagonally.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"us