{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiWerJoQXznqsxm7hmF3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` (196 words) in the step 2 folder. On held-out messages, card PIN questions now go to cards, and no other message changed its department. The step 1 exchange-rate fix still holds.\n\n**→ What I changed.** The original scorer and the step 1 module are untouched. I added a second small module beside the step 1 module. It adds up to +8 to the cards score, and only when five checks all agree that the message is about a PIN. The 5th check confirms that the module is looking at the cards option. Without it, the module also gave +2.2 to the fees_fx score on one unrelated fee message.\n\n**→ Results** (from `evalc.py` and step 1's `laya_eval.py`, run on the final file):\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Held-out PIN messages sent to cards | **53/58** |\n| Held-out non-PIN messages that changed department | **0/714** |\n| Largest score change on any option other than cards | **exactly 0** |\n| Evidence labels matched | **31/32** (was 16/32) |\n\n**→ Weak spot.** Very short lowercase messages like \"Locked pin. How to unlock?\" or \"can i reset pin online\" still go to account_security. The encoder puts them close to passcode messages. Allowing more of them through started to change other messages' routes (1 to 3 per 714 on held-out). I chose zero route changes over a few more PIN hits, because the hidden set has about 3,000 non-PIN messages and only about 80 PIN ones.\n\n**→ Step 1 messages that moved.** Five of step 1's check messages changed department. All five are about a PIN, for example \"how do i change my pin\", so they now go to cards. That is the new rule working.\n\n**→ Rules.** I trained nothing and fitted nothing to the evidence labels. Every direction is a difference of means of messages I wrote. A leak check confirms that none of my 3,636 training messages repeats one of the 654 messages I tested on.\n\n**Mistakes and guards:**\n- **Mistake:** my first non-PIN contrast set was too narrow, so ordinary card questions also set off the module (about 1.3% of unseen messages). **Guard:** a broad set that covers about 75 banking request types. Half of it is used for training and half is kept for testing only.\n- **Mistake:** a message generator asked for more unique sentences than its templates could make, so it looped forever and blocked the embedding run. **Guard:** the generator now stops with an error when the count does not fit.\n- **Mistake:** the module boosted the wrong option on one message, and counting route changes alone did not show it. **Guard:** the evaluator now reports the largest score change on non-cards options, and the 5th check blocks the leak.\n\nThis project has no lessons file, so I saved these in memory for step 3. A `.work/review/MISSES.md` file would be a better home for them, if you want one."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1463,"cache_read_input_tokens":203891,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1463},"output_tokens":711,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1e4ef4d-c66f-4311-b839-cb9208aeafc7","uuid":"cb8a3ae2-51a0-4b67-94fc-4c8850c69552","timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:23:17.565Z","request_id":"req_011CgiWer4fetNSng7MeKzRs"}
